WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Deep Anatomy of the Femoral Canal & Cloquet's Node.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The femoral canal is the innermost compartment of the femoral sheath, measuring 1.3 cm in length.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
It contains lymphatic vessels draining deep inguinal structures and the deep node of Cloquet (Rosenmüller).

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Femoral hernias pass through the unyielding femoral ring medial to the femoral vein and lateral to the lacunar ligament of Gimbernat.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Because of rigid anatomical margins, femoral hernias carry an exceptionally high risk of strangulation and require urgent operative repair.
